[1mThe test harness flaw that hid everything.[22m My first several test runs were meaningless. With [38;5;10mcrate-type = ["cdylib"][0m alone, the lib target has no dependents among the integration tests, so [38;5;10mcargo test[0m never rebuilt the [38;5;10m.so[0m — every run compared against a stale library from my initial [38;5;10mcargo build[0m. Two changes were needed: adding [38;5;10mrlib[0m to [38;5;10mcrate-type[0m and a [38;5;10muse agglom_lib as _;[0m in the harness (to make the lib a dependency of the test binaries), and pointing the loader at [38;5;10mtarget/<profile>/deps/libagglom_lib.so[0m, since cargo only "uplifts" a copy to [38;5;10mtarget/<profile>/[0m for [38;5;10mcargo build[0m, not for [38;5;10mcargo test[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe real defects — all NaN bit patterns.[22m Every mismatch came from x86 scalar SSE semantics that plain Rust arithmetic does not reproduce:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mmulss[0m/[38;5;10maddss[0m return the [1mdestination[22m operand when both operands are NaN. Since [38;5;10m+[0m and [38;5;10m*[0m are commutative, register allocation picks the result's payload — and gcc [38;5;10m-O0[0m and LLVM disagree. Reordering the Rust source does [3mnot[23m help: I verified via [38;5;10mobjdump[0m that LLVM emits identical code either way. I read the destination gcc actually chose out of the reference [38;5;10m.so[0m disassembly and encoded it explicitly in [38;5;10msse_mul(dest, src)[0m / [38;5;10msse_add(dest, src)[0m helpers, applied to [38;5;10mc2Dot[0m, [38;5;10mlm_dot2[0m, [38;5;10mf9[0m, [38;5;10mf11[0m and [38;5;10mf12[0m.[0m[0m
- An invalid operation ([38;5;10m0 * inf[0m, [38;5;10minf - inf[0m) produces the [3msign-set[23m "QNaN indefinite" [38;5;10m0xFFC00000[0m, not [38;5;10m0x7FC00000[0m. My first attempt used the positive constant and simply inverted the failures, which is what exposed this.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Non-commutative ops ([38;5;10msubss[0m, [38;5;10mdivss[0m) needed no help — their operand order is fixed, so the hardware produces identical results on both sides.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mWhat was already correct:[22m [38;5;10mf3[0m's INT_MIN floor-division dance, [38;5;10mf4[0m's bit-punned RNG, [38;5;10mf5[0m, [38;5;10mf7[0m's unsigned wraparound, [38;5;10mf10[0m's table lookup, [38;5;10mf13[0m, the [38;5;10mf2[0m dispatcher, and the 33-argument [38;5;10magglom[0m ABI. [38;5;10mf10[0m is verified exhaustively over all 65536 inputs, which also fully validates [38;5;10mtables.rs[0m — every one of the 2048 mantissa entries is reachable. [38;5;10mf12[0m's [38;5;10m(int)floorf(h)[0m cast is UB in C but the binary uses [38;5;10mcvttss2si[0m; the existing [38;5;10mc_cast_i32[0m emulation was right, and I confirmed against the disassembly that C really calls [38;5;10mfloorf[0m (not truncation) since that changes which branch is taken for negative hues.[0m[0m
